        <!-- Section 1: Prerequisites -->
        <div class="card" id="prerequisites">
            <h2>📋 1. Prerequisites</h2>
            <p>Before starting, ensure you have the following installed on your Windows laptop:</p>

            <h3>🔧 1.1 Install Node.js and npm</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Download from: <a href="https://nodejs.org/" target="_blank">https://nodejs.org/</a> (Download LTS version)</li>
                <li>Run the installer and follow the installation wizard</li>
                <li>Verify installation: Open <strong>Command Prompt</strong> or <strong>PowerShell</strong> and type:</li>
            </ul>
            <pre><code>node --version
npm --version</code></pre>

            <h3>🐘 1.2 Install PostgreSQL</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Download from: <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/download/windows/" target="_blank">https://www.postgresql.org/download/windows/</a></li>
                <li>Choose version 14 or higher</li>
                <li>During installation:
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Remember the password</strong> you set for the <code>postgres</code> user (e.g., <code>postgres123</code>)</li>
                        <li>Keep default port: <code>5432</code></li>
                        <li>Install pgAdmin (comes bundled)</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>Verify installation: Search for "pgAdmin 4" in Windows Start menu</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>📦 1.3 Install Git</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Download from: <a href="https://git-scm.com/download/win" target="_blank">https://git-scm.com/download/win</a></li>
                <li>Run installer (default settings are fine)</li>
                <li>Verify installation:</li>
            </ul>
            <pre><code>git --version</code></pre>

            <h3>💻 1.4 Install Visual Studio Code</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Download from: <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/download" target="_blank">https://code.visualstudio.com/download</a></li>
                <li>Install and launch VS Code</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2: Clone Repository -->
        <div class="card" id="clone">
            <h2>🚀 2. Clone the Repository</h2>
            <div class="step">
                <span class="step-number">1</span> Open <strong>VS Code</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <span class="step-number">2</span> Press <code>Ctrl + Shift + P</code> to open command palette
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <span class="step-number">3</span> Type <code>Git: Clone</code> and press Enter
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <span class="step-number">4</span> Enter the repository URL:
                <pre><code>https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/tscf-vision-partners.git</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <span class="step-number">5</span> Choose a folder on your computer (e.g., <code>C:\Projects\</code>)
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <span class="step-number">6</span> When prompted, click "Open" to open the cloned repository
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-info">
                <strong>💡 Alternative using Command Prompt:</strong>
                <pre><code>cd C:\Projects
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/tscf-vision-partners.git
cd tscf-vision-partners
code .</code></pre>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3: Database Setup -->
        <div class="card" id="database">
            <h2>🐘 3. Set Up PostgreSQL Database</h2>

            <h3>📀 3.1 Create Database using pgAdmin</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Open <strong>pgAdmin 4</strong> from Windows Start menu</li>
                <li>Click on "Servers" → "PostgreSQL" → Enter your password</li>
                <li>Right-click on "Databases" → "Create" → "Database"</li>
                <li>Name the database: <code>tscf_db</code></li>
                <li>Click "Save"</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>📝 3.2 Create Database Tables</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>In VS Code, open the <code>database.sql</code> file</li>
                <li>Select all content (<code>Ctrl + A</code>)</li>
                <li>Copy (<code>Ctrl + C</code>)</li>
                <li>Open pgAdmin 4</li>
                <li>Click on <code>tscf_db</code> database</li>
                <li>Click on "Query Tool" (puzzle icon or Tools → Query Tool)</li>
                <li>Paste the SQL code (<code>Ctrl + V</code>)</li>
                <li>Press <code>F5</code> or click "Execute" (lightning bolt icon)</li>
            </ol>

            <div class="alert alert-success">
                <strong>✅ Expected output:</strong> <code>CREATE TABLE</code> and <code>CREATE INDEX</code> messages
            </div>

            <h3>⚙️ 3.3 Alternative using Command Line</h3>
            <pre><code>psql -U postgres
# Enter your password when prompted
# Then run:
CREATE DATABASE tscf_db;
\q</code></pre>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4: Backend Setup -->
        <div class="card" id="backend">
            <h2>⚙️ 4. Backend Configuration & Setup</h2>

            <h3>📄 4.1 Configure Environment Variables</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>In VS Code, navigate to the <code>backend</code> folder</li>
                <li>Create a new file called <code>.env</code></li>
                <li>Add the following content (replace password with yours - I will provide the password):</li>
            </ol>
            <pre><code>DB_USER=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=postgres123
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_DATABASE=tscf_db
PORT=5000</code></pre>

            <h3>📦 4.2 Install Backend Dependencies</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Open VS Code terminal: <code>Terminal</code> → <code>New Terminal</code></li>
                <li>Navigate to backend folder:</li>
            </ol>
            <pre><code>cd backend</code></pre>
            <ol start="3">
                <li>Install dependencies:</li>
            </ol>
            <pre><code>npm install</code></pre>

            <h3>▶️ 4.3 Start the Backend Server</h3>
            <pre><code>npm run dev</code></pre>
            <div class="alert alert-success">
                <strong>✅ You should see:</strong><br>
                <code>✅ Database connected successfully<br>Server running on port 5000</code>
            </div>
            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                <strong>⚠️ Important:</strong> Keep this terminal running! Don't close it.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5: Frontend Setup -->
        <div class="card" id="frontend">
            <h2>🎨 5. Frontend Setup</h2>

            <h3>📦 5.1 Install Frontend Dependencies</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Open a <strong>new terminal</strong> in VS Code (<code>Ctrl + Shift + `</code>)</li>
                <li>Navigate to frontend folder:</li>
            </ol>
            <pre><code>cd frontend</code></pre>
            <ol start="3">
                <li>Install dependencies:</li>
            </ol>
            <pre><code>npm install</code></pre>

            <h3>▶️ 5.2 Start the Frontend Application</h3>
            <pre><code>npm start</code></pre>
            <div class="alert alert-success">
                <strong>✅ The application will automatically open in your browser at:</strong> <code>http://localhost:3000</code>
            </div>

            <h3>🧪 5.3 Test the Application</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Fill out the membership form</li>
                <li>Click "Submit Application"</li>
                <li>Click "Show Admin Panel" to see your submission</li>
                <li>Test approve/reject/delete functions</li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6: Git Workflow -->
        <div class="card" id="git-workflow">
            <h2>📝 6. Working with Git & GitHub</h2>

            <h3>🔄 Basic Git Workflow</h3>

            <h4>Pull latest changes from GitHub (do this before starting work):</h4>
            <pre><code>git pull origin main</code></pre>

            <h4>Check what files have changed:</h4>
            <pre><code>git status</code></pre>

            <h4>Add your changes:</h4>
            <pre><code># Add specific file
git add backend/server.js

# Add all changes
git add .</code></pre>

            <h4>Commit your changes (save locally):</h4>
            <pre><code>git commit -m "type: description of changes"</code></pre>

            <h4>Push to GitHub:</h4>
            <pre><code>git push origin main</code></pre>

            <h3>📝 Commit Message Guidelines</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Prefix</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>feat:</code></td><td>New feature</td><td><code>feat: added email validation to form</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fix:</code></td><td>Bug fix</td><td><code>fix: resolved database connection error</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>docs:</code></td><td>Documentation changes</td><td><code>docs: updated README with setup instructions</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>style:</code></td><td>Code style changes</td><td><code>style: formatted code with prettier</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>refactor:</code></td><td>Code restructuring</td><td><code>refactor: simplified database queries</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>test:</code></td><td>Adding tests</td><td><code>test: added unit tests for API</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>chore:</code></td><td>Maintenance tasks</td><td><code>chore: updated dependencies</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <h3>⚠️ Resolving Merge Conflicts</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>VS Code will show files with conflicts</li>
                <li>Look for <code>&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;</code>, <code>=======</code>, <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> markers</li>
                <li>Choose which changes to keep or edit manually</li>
                <li>Save the file</li>
                <li>Run:</li>
            </ol>
            <pre><code>git add .
git commit -m "resolved merge conflict"
git push</code></pre>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 7: Troubleshooting -->
        <div class="card" id="troubleshooting">
            <h2>🛠️ 7. Common Issues & Solutions</h2>

            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                <strong>❌ Issue 1:</strong> "Can't find module" errors<br>
                <strong>✅ Solution:</strong> Reinstall dependencies
                <pre><code>cd backend
rm -rf node_modules
npm install</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                <strong>❌ Issue 2:</strong> Port 3000 already in use<br>
                <strong>✅ Solution:</strong> Kill the process using the port
                <pre><code>netstat -ano | findstr :3000
taskkill /PID 12345 /F</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                <strong>❌ Issue 3:</strong> Database connection failed<br>
                <strong>✅ Solution:</strong> Check PostgreSQL is running
                <ol>
                    <li>Open "Services" app in Windows</li>
                    <li>Find "postgresql" service</li>
                    <li>Make sure it's "Running"</li>
                    <li>If not, right-click → Start</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                <strong>❌ Issue 4:</strong> Password authentication failed<br>
                <strong>✅ Solution:</strong> Update <code>.env</code> file with correct PostgreSQL password
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                <strong>❌ Issue 5:</strong> npm install is very slow<br>
                <strong>✅ Solution:</strong> Use faster download mirror
                <pre><code>npm install --registry=https://registry.npmmirror.com</code></pre>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 8: VS Code Shortcuts -->
        <div class="card" id="shortcuts">
            <h2>⌨️ 8. VS Code Shortcuts & Tips</h2>

            <h3>Essential Shortcuts</h3>
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Windows Shortcut</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Open terminal</td><td><code>Ctrl + `</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Search files</td><td><code>Ctrl + P</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Save file</td><td><code>Ctrl + S</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Find in file</td><td><code>Ctrl + F</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Find in project</td><td><code>Ctrl + Shift + F</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Open command palette</td><td><code>Ctrl + Shift + P</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Split terminal</td><td><code>Ctrl + Shift + 5</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <h3>Recommended VS Code Extensions</h3>
            <p>Install these from Extensions marketplace (<code>Ctrl + Shift + X</code>):</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>ES7+ React/Redux/React-Native snippets</strong> - React code shortcuts</li>
                <li><strong>Prettier</strong> - Code formatter</li>
                <li><strong>GitLens</strong> - Better Git integration</li>
                <li><strong>PostgreSQL</strong> - SQL syntax highlighting</li>
                <li><strong>Tailwind CSS IntelliSense</strong> - CSS suggestions</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 9: Daily Workflow -->
        <div class="card">
            <h2>🔄 Daily Development Workflow</h2>
            <pre><code># 1. Start your day - get latest changes
git pull origin main

# 2. Start backend (in one terminal)
cd backend
npm run dev

# 3. Start frontend (in another terminal)
cd frontend
npm start

# 4. Make your changes in VS Code

# 5. Test your changes in browser (http://localhost:3000)

# 6. Commit your work
git add .
git commit -m "type: description of changes"

# 7. Push to GitHub
git push origin main

# 8. Stop servers when done (Ctrl + C in each terminal)</code></pre>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 10: Project Structure -->
        <div class="card">
            <h2>📂 Project Structure to Understand</h2>
            <pre><code>tscf-vision-partners/
│
├── backend/                 # Server-side code
│   ├── server.js           # Main Express server
│   ├── db.js               # Database connection
│   ├── .env                # Environment variables (your secrets)
│   └── package.json        # Backend dependencies
│
├── frontend/                # Client-side React app
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── App.js          # Main React component (where you'll edit most)
│   │   ├── index.js        # React entry point
│   │   └── index.css       # Global styles
│   ├── public/             # Static files
│   └── package.json        # Frontend dependencies
│
├── database.sql            # Database schema (run once)
└── README.md               # Project documentation</code></pre>

            <h3>Where to Make Changes</h3>
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>What to change</th><th>Which file</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Form fields, layout</td><td><code>frontend/src/App.js</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Colors, styling</td><td><code>frontend/src/App.js</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>API endpoints</td><td><code>backend/server.js</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Database queries</td><td><code>backend/server.js</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Environment variables</td><td><code>backend/.env</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

